WEBVTT

00:07.830 --> 00:09.790
Hey, are we really going in the right direction?

00:10.120 --> 00:11.660
How would I know?

00:16.500 --> 00:17.290
Hey, look!

00:18.670 --> 00:21.510
Oh no! We came all the way to the Twin Islands!

00:30.230 --> 00:31.430
Wh-What the hell are these voices?

00:33.310 --> 00:33.770
What's wrong?

00:40.240 --> 00:41.400
They're Funayuurei!

00:46.320 --> 00:48.990
S-Save us!

00:55.000 --> 01:03.770
(Wanting you to just be near,
to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:03.810 --> 01:12.810
(Wishing you would call my name,
'Cause only you can light the flame)

01:12.850 --> 01:19.580
Constantly searching,
still can't find

01:22.190 --> 01:28.260
Ever illusive peace of mind

01:30.430 --> 01:39.000
Sometimes it's near,
but slips away

01:39.040 --> 01:45.640
And I'm faced with another day

01:46.850 --> 01:52.580
Of wanting you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:52.620 --> 01:56.920
...to just be near
('Cause only you can light the flame)

01:56.960 --> 02:01.400
Of wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

02:01.430 --> 02:05.830
...would call my name,
to feel your breath upon my ear

02:05.870 --> 02:10.360
Of wanting you... wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

02:10.410 --> 02:18.250
Call my name, 'cause only
you can light the flame

02:23.430 --> 02:23.460
Funayuurei

02:33.520 --> 02:36.020
Mataichi-san... where are you right now?

02:36.820 --> 02:37.900
Sensei!

02:40.030 --> 02:42.240
It may be time for us to part.

02:44.070 --> 02:46.080
It's been three months since then.

02:50.580 --> 02:56.790
I didn't even know anything
about where, or how, Mataichi and his group lived.

02:57.760 --> 03:02.590
All I knew was that there were
strange rumors wherever they appeared.

03:05.350 --> 03:06.300
This is...

03:08.060 --> 03:13.230
"A man capable of disguising himself
as anything... from animals, to women, to children."

03:13.560 --> 03:15.440
[Note: Rien was the first emperor of the Tang Dynasty.]

03:13.560 --> 03:15.440
"A maverick descended from Rien."

03:15.860 --> 03:17.520
[Note: Toriyose means bird caller.]

03:15.860 --> 03:17.520
A toriyose named Nagamimi?

03:17.650 --> 03:19.360
This is Nagamimi-san?

03:19.990 --> 03:21.400
Is he an acquaintance of yours?

03:26.240 --> 03:28.580
I just stopped by in hopes of finding a good book,

03:28.660 --> 03:30.660
but look who's here!

03:30.750 --> 03:31.450
All right...

03:34.710 --> 03:36.750
You know him?

03:36.960 --> 03:38.210
What if I do?

03:38.670 --> 03:41.960
I'd expect no less from a great
sensei who is trying to publish 100 stories.

03:42.130 --> 03:44.430
You even know people in the afterlife?

03:44.470 --> 03:44.930
What?

03:45.090 --> 03:49.010
If he were still alive, he'd be over 200 years old.

03:50.600 --> 03:51.470
It's true!

03:52.140 --> 03:55.060
Looks like you're in too deep to come back out, sensei.

03:55.600 --> 04:01.070
U-Umm... do you know of any strange
rumors that have been spreading recently?

04:01.940 --> 04:03.440
Strange rumors, huh?

04:05.070 --> 04:10.910
Shichininmisaki of Kitabayashi
province and Funayuurei of Sanuki province.

04:12.370 --> 04:15.580
Shichininmisaki and Funayuurei, huh?

04:31.350 --> 04:34.750
Kyougokutei

04:35.270 --> 04:36.100
A tea house?

04:36.560 --> 04:37.650
In a place like this?

04:49.200 --> 04:51.280
We've been waiting for you, sensei.

04:51.450 --> 04:53.540
At last we meet, sensei.

04:54.660 --> 04:56.040
How do you know about me?

04:56.290 --> 04:59.000
We have heard everything from Mataichi.

04:59.080 --> 05:01.590
And we have heard from Ogin and Nagamimi, as well.

05:01.750 --> 05:02.800
Then, you are...

05:03.170 --> 05:07.180
Those three are always helping us out.

05:08.590 --> 05:13.100
I'm the master of this place; Kyougokutei.

05:13.600 --> 05:14.770
Kyougokutei...

05:15.180 --> 05:17.310
Could you be Mataichi-san's groups...?

05:17.560 --> 05:20.230
It's better to not say anymore about that.

05:20.360 --> 05:21.980
Better to say no more on that.

05:22.150 --> 05:28.280
It has been a great help for us to have a
respectable person like you aid us, sensei.

05:28.450 --> 05:31.740
No, I just do what I'm told.

05:31.910 --> 05:34.290
That's not true.

05:34.410 --> 05:34.830
What?

05:35.330 --> 05:38.710
Ever since you joined the group,
each setup has gone very smoothly.

05:38.870 --> 05:42.090
In addition, we now have some class.

05:42.590 --> 05:44.050
R-Really?

05:44.130 --> 05:47.010
But they're really having difficulties this time.

05:47.170 --> 05:49.590
Just as we've thought,
it just won't work without you, sensei.

05:50.090 --> 05:51.590
Where did Mataichi-san go?

05:52.300 --> 05:54.970
He went to Shikoku island,
but now we don't know where he is.

05:55.310 --> 05:56.720
We can't contact him, either.

05:57.350 --> 06:01.100
Shikoku? That's where the
rumored Funayuurei in Sanuki province are.

06:01.400 --> 06:04.860
How worrisome.

06:12.450 --> 06:14.870
They say the Funayuurei showed up again?

06:15.700 --> 06:17.500
It was around Helm Island, apparently...

06:17.710 --> 06:21.210
They say that the ship was torn to pieces,
and they couldn't save a single person!

06:21.710 --> 06:23.670
We can't go fishing when things are like this.

06:23.750 --> 06:27.920
Umm... did the Funayuurei sink that boat?

06:28.010 --> 06:29.840
It's been happening a lot around here, recently.

06:30.050 --> 06:32.970
Attacking ships... that's like something a pirate would do.

06:33.390 --> 06:35.180
But isn't it strange?

06:35.640 --> 06:38.220
The Funayuurei are supposed to
show up around the Twin Islands.

06:38.430 --> 06:40.520
Why did they appear near Helm Island?

06:41.190 --> 06:42.560
Now that you mention it...

06:42.650 --> 06:44.020
What do you mean?

06:44.360 --> 06:47.980
About half a day from here by boat, there used to
be two linear islands that we called the Twin Islands.

06:48.070 --> 06:54.990
Then, one night, about twenty
years ago, one of them suddenly disappeared.

06:55.080 --> 06:56.680
An entire island disappeared in a single night?

06:57.040 --> 06:59.600
We always had rumors saying
that there were Funayuurei around here,

06:59.750 --> 07:04.500
but ever since the island disappeared, it's been said that
the Funayuurei tend to appear around the Twin Islands.

07:07.170 --> 07:10.380
Funayuurei are the ghosts of those who perished at sea,

07:10.800 --> 07:12.760
and have returned to haunt the living.

07:13.640 --> 07:17.600
The dead approach you on boats
and ask you to lend them a ladle.

07:18.020 --> 07:23.480
It's said that if you do, they'll
ladle seawater into your ship and sink it.

07:24.610 --> 07:25.940
Y-You've got to hear this!

07:27.070 --> 07:30.320
Sekiyama-sama, the ship's
management magistrate himself, has come!

07:39.870 --> 07:42.160
There is no need for formalities. Raise your faces.

07:46.130 --> 07:47.090
Well, I suppose it'll do.

07:47.630 --> 07:52.220
The Funayuurei's disasters that have recently
plagued this place are not supernatural events.

07:52.630 --> 07:55.220
We have deemed it all to be the Kawakubo clan's doing.

07:56.640 --> 08:00.180
We cannot possibly forgive them for
threatening the fishermen's livelihood.

08:01.100 --> 08:03.480
Thus, we have decided to eradicate them.

08:06.730 --> 08:10.110
Is that so? You met Sekiyama-sama, huh?

08:10.570 --> 08:12.780
He seems like a very respectable person.

08:13.030 --> 08:14.950
He really is, they say.

08:15.820 --> 08:17.740
About what I heard then...

08:17.990 --> 08:20.950
Who are the Kawakubo clan?

08:21.120 --> 08:21.580
What?

08:22.080 --> 08:24.160
No one down at the shore would tell me.

08:24.420 --> 08:25.710
I-Is that so?

08:25.960 --> 08:27.170
Do you know anything?

08:27.380 --> 08:29.750
Wh-Who knows? Enjoy your stay!

08:32.760 --> 08:34.380
I-I don't know anything.

08:36.220 --> 08:40.890
None of the villagers would tell
me anything about the Kawakubo clan.

08:48.860 --> 08:49.860
Hey, you.

08:49.980 --> 08:50.610
Yes?

08:51.110 --> 08:54.610
You're going around asking
about the Kawakubo clan, aren't you?

08:55.950 --> 08:57.660
What? You can't answer?

08:58.490 --> 08:59.530
Ah well.

08:59.740 --> 09:02.160
Whether or not you answer our
question, we will still cut you down.

09:16.510 --> 09:17.300
This is...

09:32.270 --> 09:34.030
Damn it! Where'd he go?!

09:34.610 --> 09:35.570
Find him!

09:38.280 --> 09:39.410
Where is he?

09:44.700 --> 09:48.580
Geez... you're such a troublemaker.

09:49.170 --> 09:50.710
I've been looking you all this time.

09:52.210 --> 09:54.800
Nobody asked you to do that.

09:55.460 --> 09:59.130
Why didn't you let me help you set up this time?

09:59.760 --> 10:00.890
Don't you get it?

10:01.510 --> 10:04.640
You're just in the way, sensei.

10:05.560 --> 10:06.640
B-But, that's--

10:07.350 --> 10:10.020
Is it because I failed last time?

10:12.020 --> 10:16.190
But that was because Mataichi-san
didn't tell me the truth beforehand.

10:16.280 --> 10:17.570
That's not it.

10:17.820 --> 10:18.320
Huh?

10:18.570 --> 10:21.700
We live in different worlds, Sensei.

10:22.160 --> 10:23.870
Then, let's live in the same--

10:24.080 --> 10:24.370
Stop it!

10:25.580 --> 10:29.370
There is a line that cannot be
crossed between human beings.

10:30.290 --> 10:35.290
Sensei... you're someone who must not enter this world...

10:36.510 --> 10:37.420
Ever.

10:40.300 --> 10:42.220
Don't get involved any further and go back to Edo

10:42.890 --> 10:43.590
Got it?

10:47.470 --> 10:48.390
Ogin-san!

10:56.230 --> 10:56.900
You!

10:57.230 --> 10:59.690
The girl you were with set sail for sea.

11:00.860 --> 11:02.570
She was heading to the Twin Islands, it seems.

11:04.870 --> 11:06.030
I have a request.

11:09.580 --> 11:13.790
Why won't anyone tell me about the Kawakubo clan?

11:15.710 --> 11:17.210
Because they're ghosts.

11:17.800 --> 11:18.670
Ghosts?

11:19.420 --> 11:25.850
[Note: The Heike clan was defeated in a famous clan war with the
Genji clan for supremacy in Japan in the late 12th Century.]

11:19.420 --> 11:22.300
The Kawakubo clan is the remnants of the Heike clan.

11:23.050 --> 11:25.850
In this day and age, the terms "Heike"
and "Genji" no longer have any meaning.

11:26.310 --> 11:28.470
Everyone's only thinking about their own well being.

11:29.310 --> 11:30.020
All the same...

11:30.310 --> 11:31.600
those people..

11:32.600 --> 11:34.560
They live in different worlds...?

11:36.690 --> 11:37.480
You can see it now!

11:38.530 --> 11:39.820
That is the Twin Islands!

11:50.910 --> 11:52.410
Oh no! If they keep holding onto the boat...

12:16.990 --> 12:19.160
I-I survived?

12:19.660 --> 12:21.200
Who the hell are you?!

12:24.500 --> 12:28.120
We can't let anyone who's seen us return alive!

12:29.920 --> 12:30.790
Are you fools?!

12:33.500 --> 12:34.590
Mataichi-san?

12:34.880 --> 12:36.460
If we let him live...

12:36.880 --> 12:39.760
No one can take another's life.

12:40.180 --> 12:42.470
But what happened twenty years ago will happen again!

12:42.550 --> 12:43.180
Shut up!

12:45.930 --> 12:47.640
I'm sorry, young one.

12:48.230 --> 12:52.610
There's supposed to be someone else
here who brought me to this place...

12:53.020 --> 12:53.900
Look at those waves.

12:54.360 --> 12:55.610
He's no longer alive.

12:57.490 --> 12:59.820
The sea is furious.

13:17.090 --> 13:23.220
[Note: The Genpei War (1179-1185) was the
clan war between the Heike and Genji clans.]

13:17.090 --> 13:21.760
The water of these shores was stained
bright with blood during the Genpei War, I hear.

13:23.890 --> 13:29.810
What's mere is... the neighboring island sank
twenty years ago, and many people died in a single night.

13:38.780 --> 13:41.110
We're the Funayuurei, you say?

13:42.070 --> 13:44.240
I see. Indeed, that may be so.

13:45.160 --> 13:47.080
However, we are not pirates!

13:47.740 --> 13:52.830
I think you should meet the magistrate
Sekiyama-sama, and clear yourself of those charges.

13:53.170 --> 13:54.710
We can't do that.

13:55.170 --> 13:55.920
But...

13:56.880 --> 13:59.010
I can't go anywhere.

14:02.010 --> 14:04.930
You're the second person to get washed up on this island.

14:05.180 --> 14:07.760
Another person was washed ashore twenty years ago.

14:08.020 --> 14:09.890
Thanks to him, we...!

14:10.680 --> 14:11.850
You're wrong.

14:13.400 --> 14:16.650
The real villain wasn't the one who was washed up.

14:17.860 --> 14:19.400
It's that.

14:21.110 --> 14:22.150
What in the world is that?

14:22.740 --> 14:26.870
When our ancestors,
the Heike clan, mobilized under the Heike banner,

14:26.950 --> 14:31.290
they entrusted this "Hikasou" to
our predecessors, telling them to make use of it.

14:31.910 --> 14:32.790
Hikasou?

14:33.330 --> 14:37.420
If it were to be used, it could upset the very heavens.

14:37.670 --> 14:39.960
You should just destroy it.

14:40.550 --> 14:42.170
But we can't.

14:43.220 --> 14:48.050
It causes disasters... It calls
forth the darkness of the human heart.

14:48.640 --> 14:49.720
I know.

14:50.350 --> 14:52.180
That is why we will never allow
it to be unleashed upon the world,

14:52.890 --> 14:54.440
but we can't destroy it anymore.

15:09.790 --> 15:12.700
If you keep to this path,
you'll emerge at the other shore of this island.

15:13.290 --> 15:15.000
Use the ship there to return.

15:15.540 --> 15:16.750
I'm not going back.

15:17.000 --> 15:19.040
You shouldn't get involved here, sensei.

15:19.590 --> 15:21.550
What do you intend to do?

15:24.510 --> 15:25.930
It's Taroumaru-san, isn't it?

15:26.340 --> 15:29.140
Your target this time is Taroumaru-san, isn't it?

15:30.060 --> 15:31.930
He hasn't done anything!

15:32.470 --> 15:34.270
That is his sin.

15:34.690 --> 15:39.900
Even if he couldn't help but to
inherit the Hikasou, to not destroy it is a sin.

15:40.110 --> 15:42.780
Does Kyougokutei know about this?

15:44.070 --> 15:45.820
How do you know about him?

15:45.990 --> 15:47.200
I met him in Edo.

15:47.610 --> 15:49.870
He's your leader, isn't he?

15:50.620 --> 15:54.500
No... Well, I thought he was,

15:55.040 --> 15:58.170
but he has begun to think of something terrible.

16:00.170 --> 16:05.670
Instead of quelling the darkness in
people's hearts, he's trying to bring it to the surface.

16:05.920 --> 16:08.680
The Hikasou is perfect for that purpose.

16:09.300 --> 16:10.010
They're here!

16:17.640 --> 16:18.440
Hyougo!

16:19.650 --> 16:23.690
The person who was washed
ashore twenty years ago was him.

16:27.950 --> 16:30.700
Taroumaru-dono, it's been a long time.

16:30.950 --> 16:32.450
Why have you returned?

16:33.160 --> 16:37.210
Members of the Kawakubo clan have been
deemed as outlaws and are wanted by the magistrate.

16:37.540 --> 16:38.710
That's nonsense.

16:39.290 --> 16:41.580
I get it. Your target is the Hikasou, correct?

16:41.880 --> 16:45.550
If you know that, than we have
little to talk about. Hand over the plans.

16:45.800 --> 16:46.460
I refuse.

16:46.970 --> 16:50.550
If I wanted to, I could kill you all and take the Hikasou.

16:51.050 --> 16:54.100
Without the plans, you wouldn't know how to make one.

16:54.680 --> 16:57.600
If I can take one of its shells back,
I can investigate the method of making it.

16:59.900 --> 17:05.530
If you give me the plans, I will clear the
Kawakubo clan of suspicion and deem you free.

17:07.820 --> 17:08.820
That man!

17:08.990 --> 17:09.990
I get it...

17:10.160 --> 17:13.820
The ones who were acting like
pirates in the Funayuurei's name were...

17:14.200 --> 17:16.330
One more word and you're a dead man!

17:17.200 --> 17:19.410
Who's the dead man here? I wonder.

17:19.750 --> 17:20.960
What's that?

17:21.290 --> 17:23.580
The Hikasou is here.

17:26.340 --> 17:29.880
You should know its power quite well.

17:40.140 --> 17:42.270
My dreams have been
disturbed by its presence so many times...

17:42.650 --> 17:45.940
And then, one day, I began to
want it so much that I couldn't take it!

17:46.230 --> 17:47.940
You became possessed, huh?

17:48.360 --> 17:50.860
You don't really intend to
fight the entire province, do you?

17:51.360 --> 17:53.360
That could be interesting.

17:53.870 --> 17:55.990
You won't get off of this island alive.

17:57.790 --> 17:59.910
Give me some time.

18:00.710 --> 18:02.250
I'll wait until dawn.

18:02.880 --> 18:04.960
Make up your mind by then.

18:07.590 --> 18:08.960
What are you going to do?

18:09.670 --> 18:11.260
Exterminate it...

18:11.630 --> 18:13.800
the monster called "Hikasou".

18:17.180 --> 18:18.810
Boss, we will...

18:18.970 --> 18:21.480
You must not waste your lives.

18:21.640 --> 18:23.190
Then, come with us!

18:23.270 --> 18:24.270
I cannot do that.

18:25.020 --> 18:27.480
I must put an end to this.

18:27.650 --> 18:29.730
Can't you just destroy it?

18:32.700 --> 18:34.860
I am now a Hikasou...

18:35.160 --> 18:39.990
and if I were to leave this place, the souls
that rest beneath the waves would become lonely.

18:41.120 --> 18:43.750
You must not waste your lives.

18:50.960 --> 18:53.590
If I had just done this sooner...

18:58.850 --> 19:01.810
When I was made to bear this burden upon my back...

19:02.850 --> 19:03.680
Stop!

19:03.890 --> 19:05.140
Please, stop this!

19:06.190 --> 19:09.190
Taroumaru, you are the next boss!

19:09.360 --> 19:11.730
No! I don't want to be!

19:12.190 --> 19:14.780
Stop!

19:16.110 --> 19:17.700
You're a coward, Father!

19:18.080 --> 19:19.910
We will cut our ties to the Kawakubi clan,

19:20.290 --> 19:23.750
and end the protection of that thing at your generation!

19:24.120 --> 19:26.830
We younger men will live on that island!

19:33.920 --> 19:38.430
If I had managed to stop him with
brute force, that wouldn't have happened...

19:47.690 --> 19:48.650
Did they run?

19:54.070 --> 19:56.950
Wait for me. I'm coming to you now!

20:53.460 --> 20:54.550
Taroumaru-sama!

20:56.760 --> 20:57.970
The boss has...

21:02.260 --> 21:04.850
The deed is done!

21:09.350 --> 21:11.440
You call this your deed?!

21:12.190 --> 21:13.810
What's wrong?

21:14.270 --> 21:18.190
Even though you make it seem
like the work of spirits and demons,

21:18.360 --> 21:19.990
what you're doing is murder, isn't it?!

21:20.610 --> 21:22.160
Why are you saying this now?

21:22.490 --> 21:25.910
And haven't you been doing this as well?

21:37.010 --> 21:37.630
That was...

21:37.800 --> 21:39.050
The same as this.

21:39.260 --> 21:42.430
They were monsters that harbored darkness in their hearts

21:42.590 --> 21:44.970
N-No, they were all humans!

21:45.220 --> 21:48.890
If that's so, have you been killing humans?

21:53.310 --> 21:55.480
Mata no ji, look at that ship.

22:01.070 --> 22:02.280
Those hags...

22:02.950 --> 22:04.780
Where do they intend to carry that thing?

22:05.120 --> 22:06.870
They can only be going to one place.

22:07.080 --> 22:08.370
Kitabayashi Province...

22:16.000 --> 22:22.090
Wind chimes whisper
soft and sweet

22:23.440 --> 22:29.530
Though there's not
a hint of a breeze

22:30.510 --> 22:36.280
Moonlight dancing
on the garden walk

22:36.320 --> 22:42.950
As it gently drifts
through the trees

22:44.320 --> 22:50.260
Romance takes flight
on this perfect night

22:50.300 --> 22:56.960
While all of the world
lays sleeping

22:57.800 --> 23:07.270
Find us here as we feel
the moment of love

23:08.580 --> 23:11.780
Draw near

23:12.050 --> 23:19.050
Dream, sleep,
with your hand in mine

23:19.090 --> 23:25.030
Underneath a blanket of stars

23:27.200 --> 23:32.470
Song birds singing
in a distant glade

23:32.510 --> 23:41.140
As we share
the warmth of the dawn

23:49.250 --> 23:53.800
Evil and ambition scatter into the darkness.
All that remains is a dubious rumor among the townsfolk.

23:54.470 --> 23:56.540
One possesses and kills seven.

23:56.800 --> 23:59.370
Those seven then again possess and kill seven each.

23:59.450 --> 24:01.550
Kitabayashi, where the land is deeply cursed.

24:01.850 --> 24:04.680
The unceasing curses mimic carnage depicting prints.

24:05.180 --> 24:09.190
On the next Kyougoku Natsuhiko's Rumors: 100 Stories,

24:09.730 --> 24:13.400
Shinigami, or rather, Shichininmisaki, Part 1.

24:14.030 --> 24:16.110
The deed is done.
